From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:01:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bash: fix the undefined behavior of six places

Add package patches for six faults of bash 5.3, none fixed in bash's
devel branch (1c20880e, 2026-09-23):

- 100: make_command clears the flags of every command through a
  SIMPLE_COM pointer, larger than the group or subshell structure it
  points to.
- 101: parse_comsub restores extglob from a local it never set, when
  parsing a command substitution changes the compatibility level.
- 102: array_value_internal goes on with an array that expanding its
  subscript unset, freed or gave another type: freed memory, or an index
  it never computed.
- 103: split_at_delims leaves the word counts unset for a string of
  whitespace delimiters, and COMP_CWORD gets an indeterminate value.
- 104: do_redirection_internal restores a word's flags from a variable
  never set, when expanding the word turns posix mode on.
- 105: pushd -N overflows a subtraction for N = INTMAX_MIN.

Found reviewing the -O3 build's warnings of bash (docs/undefined-behavior.md),
100 to 104 among them and 105 next to them.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
